From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Let a chip set the default PM2 sleep
 return

cfg80211 hands set_power_mgmt() a timeout of -1 unless wext set one,
and nl80211 has no way to set it, so in practice the timeout is always
-1. The driver feeds that through min_t(u32, ...), which turns it into
the 2000 ms cap: with power save on, every frame keeps the radio awake
for two seconds afterwards.

Treat a negative timeout as "no preference" and ask the chip for its
default. No chip has one yet, so this keeps 2000 ms everywhere.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c        | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 92226e646a..fdd00e0820 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -3475,6 +3475,20 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_dump_station(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 	return -ENOENT;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The PM2 sleep return is how long the firmware keeps the radio awake after
+ * the last frame before it naps again. cfg80211 passes -1 when nobody set a
+ * timeout, which is the normal case: only wext can set one. Let a chip say
+ * what that default is; everything else keeps the longest return.
+ */
+static u32 brcmf_ps_default_timeout(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
+{
+	switch (drvr->bus_if->chip) {
+	default:
+		return BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS;
+	}
+}
+
 static s32
 brcmf_cfg80211_set_power_mgmt(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev,
 			   bool enabled, s32 timeout)
@@ -3518,6 +3532,7 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_set_power_mgmt(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev,
 	}
 
 	err = brcmf_fil_iovar_int_set(ifp, "pm2_sleep_ret",
+				timeout < 0 ? brcmf_ps_default_timeout(drvr) :
 				min_t(u32, timeout, BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS));
 	if (err)
 		bphy_err(drvr, "Unable to set pm timeout, (%d)\n", err);
-- 
